// (Tani, Physics Today 1989); silver bromide is sensitive mainly to blue light, so black-and-white paper is
// handled under a red or amber safelight. Exposure times are flagged as a model (the first plates needed
// several minutes in bright light, seconds by the 1840s with faster lenses and accelerators). Placeholders:
